<header><h1>The Mahact Gene&ndash;Sorcerers: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/F_mahact">The Mahact Gene&ndash;Sorcerers</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2 id="edict"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mahact_Gene-Sorcerers#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Edict">Edict</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>When the Mahact player wins a space combat, they add the command token to their fleet pool before they resolve fleet pool requirements.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If an agenda requires the Mahact player to remove one of their command tokens from their fleet pool, and they only have other players&rsquo; command tokens in their fleet pool, they must remove one of those tokens, and return it to the reinforcements of the player that owns it.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If you are the Mahact player, what happens when an agenda tells you to &lsquo;remove one of your command tokens from your fleet pool &hellip;&rsquo; but you only have tokens from&rdquo; other players? &ldquo;A: You are required to remove another player&rsquo;s token and return it to that player&rsquo;s reinforcements.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Armed Forces Standardization affect Mahact holding other players&rsquo; fleet tokens?&rdquo;: &ldquo;other players&rsquo; tokens removed go back to their owners&rsquo; reinforcements.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Fleet%20Regulations"><i>Fleet Regulations</i></a> law limits the number of tokens the Mahact player may have in their fleet pool, they may still add a command token to their fleet pool when they are at the limit, but must then remove one command token and return it to the corresponding reinforcements.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If the law Fleet Regulations is in play, and Mahact already has 4 tokens in fleet, can they add another one &hellip;? A: The Mahact player can add a 5th token and choose one to return to their reinforcements from their fleet pool afterward.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Mahact player wins a combat against a player that has no command tokens in their reinforcements, and none of their command tokens are on the Mahact player&rsquo;s command sheet, that player must choose one of their command tokens on their command sheet to remove and place on the Mahact player&rsquo;s command sheet.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If a player has no command tokens in their reinforcements or on their command sheet, the Mahact player cannot place one of that player&rsquo;s command tokens on their command sheet if they win a combat against that player.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If the Mahact player is required to place a command token from their reinforcements on the board, such as when they retreat from a space combat, or the primary ability of the <a href="/R_diplomacy"><i>Diplomacy</i></a> strategy card, if they have no tokens in their reinforcements, they must use a Mahact token from any pool of their command sheet, and not another player&rsquo;s token in their fleet pool.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Mahact player wins a combat against the <a href="/F_mentak">Mentak</a> player and gains one of their command tokens, they cannot resolve the ability of <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Leaders:~:text=S%27ula%20Mentarion">S&rsquo;ula Mentarion</a>, the <a href="/F_mentak">Mentak</a> commander, from winning that same combat to take a promissory note from the <a href="/F_mentak">Mentak</a> player.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found. Owner ruling (2026-11-21): S&rsquo;ula Mentarion triggers &ldquo;after you win a space combat&rdquo;; the Mahact player only gains access to it through Edict as a result of winning that combat, so the commander was not available when its trigger occurred.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="imperia"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mahact_Gene-Sorcerers#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Imperia">Imperia</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="hubris"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mahact_Gene-Sorcerers#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Hubris">Hubris</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If a game effect would force another player to give a promissory note to the Mahact player, but the only promissory note that player has is their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Alliance"><i>Alliance</i></a> promissory note, that player does not give anything to the Mahact player.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="scepter-of-dominion"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mahact_Gene-Sorcerers#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Scepter%20of%20Dominion">Scepter of Dominion</a> <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If a player already has a command token in the chosen system, they do not place a command token there.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 32.2b (Diplomacy): &ldquo;If a player already has a command token in the chosen system, they do not place a command token there.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player has no command tokens in their reinforcements, that player places one command token of their choice from their command sheet.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 32.2a (Diplomacy): &ldquo;If a player has no command tokens in their reinforcements, that player places one command token of their choice from their command sheet.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Mahact player will also place a command token in the chosen system, unless their command sheet has none of their own tokens on it.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li><i>Scepter of Dominion</i> cannot place command tokens in the home system of an eliminated player.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus, &ldquo;What happens to Avernus if Muaat is eliminated?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Avernus, its token, planet card and legendary ability remain in play. Similar to an eliminated faction&rsquo;s home system.&rdquo; An eliminated player&rsquo;s home system stays a home system.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="genetic-recombination"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mahact_Gene-Sorcerers#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Genetic%20Recombination">Genetic Recombination</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A player that cannot vote due to a game effect or because they have zero influence on readied planets cannot be targeted by <i>Genetic Recombination</i>.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Genetic Recombination happens before a player would exhaust planets to vote. So if a player cannot vote, or does not have votes to cast, they cannot be targeted by the tech.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can Genetic Recombination target a player who isn&rsquo;t voting, such as one who played a rider?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; it triggers before a player casts votes, and a non-voter never reaches that point.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If a player then gains the ability to vote, they may then be targeted by <i>Genetic Recombination</i>.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If they obtain an ability that would allow them to vote, they could be targeted by the tech before the votes are cast.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="crimson-legionnaire"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mahact_Gene-Sorcerers#Infantry:~:text=Crimson%20Legionnaire">Crimson Legionnaire</a> <sub>(Unit)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If multiple Crimson Legionnaires are destroyed at the same time, the Mahact player decides whether to gain a commodity or convert a commodity to a trade good individually for each.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;If several Crimson Legionnaires die at once, does each trigger separately?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; each has its own trigger, resolved one after another.&rdquo; each triggers separately, so the choice is made per Legionnaire.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If two Crimson Legionnaires are destroyed at the same time, the Mahact player may choose to gain a commodity, then immediately convert that commodity to a trade good.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;If several Crimson Legionnaires die at once, does each trigger separately?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; each has its own trigger, resolved one after another.&rdquo; triggers resolve one after another, so a gained commodity can then be converted by the next.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="arvicon-rex"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mahact_Gene-Sorcerers#Flagship:~:text=Arvicon%20Rex">Arvicon Rex</a> <sub>(Flagship)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="jae-mir-kan"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mahact_Gene-Sorcerers#Leaders:~:text=Jae%20Mir%20Kan">Jae Mir Kan</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Jae Mir Kan may be used even if the Mahact player has no command tokens in their strategy pool.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can the Mahact agent, or other effects used instead of spending a strategy token, work with an empty strategy pool?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; they replace the token, so none is needed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Mahact player has the <a href="/F_muaat">Muaat</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Alliance"><i>Alliance</i></a> promissory note, they will not gain a trade good from it when they use the ability of Jae Mir Kan.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="il-na-viroset"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mahact_Gene-Sorcerers#Leaders:~:text=Il%20Na%20Viroset">Il Na Viroset</a> <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Mahact player cannot use any &ldquo;when/after you activate a system&rdquo; abilities.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;In regards to the Mahact Commander, Il Na Viroset, when does your turn end? &hellip; Is this different from Nullification Field or Starlancer? A: &hellip; when/after you activate and other abilities within your turn cannot be used when the Mahact player places a second token in a system. End of turn abilities can still be used. Any ability that ends your turn should be treated as ending your turn when they occur, and no further abilities during that same trigger window can take place.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can I use Scanlink Drone Network or other activation abilities when activating a system with the Mahact commander?&rdquo;: &ldquo;the commander ends your turn as part of resolving it, so no window for other abilities opens&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>Other players cannot use any &ldquo;when/after another player activates a system that&hellip;&rdquo; abilities.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;In regards to the Mahact Commander, Il Na Viroset, when does your turn end? &hellip; Is this different from Nullification Field or Starlancer? A: &hellip; when/after you activate and other abilities within your turn cannot be used when the Mahact player places a second token in a system. End of turn abilities can still be used. Any ability that ends your turn should be treated as ending your turn when they occur, and no further abilities during that same trigger window can take place.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can I use Scanlink Drone Network or other activation abilities when activating a system with the Mahact commander?&rdquo;: &ldquo;the commander ends your turn as part of resolving it, so no window for other abilities opens&rdquo; No window opens for any player.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If the Mahact player activates a system containing another player&rsquo;s units, they must still return any promissory notes with such an activation as the return condition.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>The Mahact player may still use any &ldquo;at the end of your turn&rdquo; abilities.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;In regards to the Mahact Commander, Il Na Viroset, when does your turn end? &hellip; Is this different from Nullification Field or Starlancer? A: &hellip; when/after you activate and other abilities within your turn cannot be used when the Mahact player places a second token in a system. End of turn abilities can still be used. Any ability that ends your turn should be treated as ending your turn when they occur, and no further abilities during that same trigger window can take place.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Mahact player places a second command token in a system using Il Na Viroset, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Codex_I:~:text=Counterstroke"><i>Counterstroke</i></a> action card cannot be played.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;What&rsquo;s the interaction with the Mahact Commander, Il Na Viroset, and the Counterstroke action card? A: Counterstroke cannot be played.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can I play Counterstroke on a system I activate that already has my command token?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Mahact&rsquo;s commander doesn&rsquo;t help either, since activating that way ends your turn at once with no after-activation abilities&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Mahact player places a second command token in a system using Il Na Viroset, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Dark_Energy_Tap"><i>Dark Energy Tap</i></a> technology does not trigger.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does Dark Energy Tap trigger if you used the Mahact Commander, Il Na Viroset? A: No.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="airo-shir-aur"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mahact_Gene-Sorcerers#Leaders:~:text=Airo%20Shir%20Aur">Airo Shir Aur</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mahact_Gene-Sorcerers#Leaders:~:text=Benediction">Benediction</a> <sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the Mahact player moves another player&rsquo;s ships, ground forces on planets are left behind.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does the Mahact hero&rsquo;s Benediction work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;move all units in its space area.&rdquo; Ground forces on planets are not in the space area.</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When using the Mahact Hero, Benediction, can the Mahact player transport other players&rsquo; ground forces from planets? Can the units&rsquo; owner transport ground forces from planets? A: No in both circumstances.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>If the Mahact player moves their own ships, they may transport ground forces on planets.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When using the Mahact Hero, Benediction, can the Mahact player transport their own ground forces from planets when moving? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If the Mahact player moves the <a href="/F_saar">Saar</a> player&rsquo;s units, any Floating Factories in the origin system will also be moved.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does the Mahact hero&rsquo;s Benediction work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;move all units in its space area (fighters, ground forces in space and Saar docks included).&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>Abilities that trigger on ships moving resolve according to their wording:<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>Abilities that trigger when a player moves ships trigger from the perspective of the Mahact player.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>Abilities that trigger when a player&rsquo;s ships move trigger from the perspective of the player that owns them.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>Abilities that trigger when a player moves their own ships trigger for the Mahact player only if the ships moved are their own. They do not trigger for a player whose ships the Mahact player moved.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>The Mahact player may move another player&rsquo;s ships into an asteroid field only if that player owns the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Antimass_Deflectors"><i>Antimass Deflectors</i></a> technology.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does the Mahact hero&rsquo;s Benediction work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;The moved ships&rsquo; owner must be able to enter that system, so no pushing them into asteroid fields or supernovas they can&rsquo;t enter.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Mahact player may move another player&rsquo;s ships into a supernova only if that player owns the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Embers_of_Muaat#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Magmus%20Reactor"><i>Magmus Reactor</i></a> <a href="/F_muaat">Muaat</a> factional technology.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does the Mahact hero&rsquo;s Benediction work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;no pushing them into asteroid fields or supernovas they can&rsquo;t enter.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Who can move into or through a supernova?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Magmus Reactor lets ships move into and stop in one.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <!--li>The Mahact player may only move the <a href="/F_empyrean">Empyrean</a> player&rsquo;s ships into a nebula.</li-->
    <li>If the Mahact player moves a player&rsquo;s ships out of a gravity rift, that player must roll for removal.<sup>3,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Do ships roll when moving out of a gravity rift due to the Mahact Hero, Benediction? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play: &ldquo;A ship that moves through or out of a gravity rift applies +1 to its move value and then rolls one die.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If the Mahact player is moving the <a href="/F_vuilraith">Vuil&rsquo;raith</a> player&rsquo;s ships out of a system containing a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Dimensional%20Tear">Dimensional Tear</a>, the <a href="/F_vuilraith">Vuil&rsquo;raith</a> player will not roll for removal.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>The Mahact player cannot move the <a href="/F_creuss">Creuss</a> player&rsquo;s ships from a system with an alpha wormhole into a system with a beta wormhole (and no alpha wormhole), or vice versa.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does the Mahact hero&rsquo;s Benediction work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Creuss&rsquo;s alpha-beta adjacency can&rsquo;t be used.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Mahact player moves the <a href="/F_muaat">Muaat</a> player&rsquo;s war sun, the <a href="/F_muaat">Muaat</a> player cannot trigger their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Embers_of_Muaat#Leaders:~:text=Nova%20Seed"><i>Nova Seed</i></a> hero ability.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The system the combat is taking place in is considered the active system during that combat.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The combat system is treated as the active system during that combat.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The player whose ships were moved is considered to be the attacker, the other player is considered to be the defender.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The ships being moved belong to the &lsquo;attacker&rsquo; and the ships not being moved belong to the &lsquo;defender.&rsquo;&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When using the Mahact Hero, Benediction, if another player&rsquo;s fleet is moved into a Mahact fleet, who is the attacker/defender? A: The player that is moved is the attacker, the player that is moved into is the defender.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>Regardless of which of the two players in combat is the attacker and which is the defender, the next player in initiative order will resolve abilities first, after the Mahact player.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>After the ships are moved, capacity is checked before the space combat begins.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;When using the Mahact Hero, Benediction, is capacity resolved after moving ships before the space combat? &hellip; A: A Capacity check is resolved before the space combat begins.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Resolving <i>Benediction</i> is not a tactical action. The <b>Activation</b>, <b>Movement</b>, <b>Invasion</b> and <b>Production</b> steps are not resolved.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>Any abilities that occur &ldquo;when/after you/another player activate a system&rdquo; will not trigger.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>The <b>Space Cannon Offense</b> substep is not resolved.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>Either player in the combat may score the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion_3:~:text=Brave%20the%20Void"><i>Brave the Void</i></a>, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion_3:~:text=Darken%20the%20Skies"><i>Darken the Skies</i></a>, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion_3:~:text=Demonstrate%20Your%20Power"><i>Demonstrate Your Power</i></a>, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition_3:~:text=Destroy%20their%20Greatest%20Ship"><i>Destroy Their Greatest Ship</i></a>, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion_3:~:text=Fight%20with%20Precision"><i>Fight with Precision</i></a>, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition_3:~:text=Spark%20a%20Rebellion"><i>Spark a Rebellion</i></a>, or <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition_3:~:text=Unveil%20Flagship"><i>Unveil Flagship</i></a> secret objectives.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>The Mahact player cannot score these secret objectives unless they are participating in the combat.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>No player may score the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion_3:~:text=Betray%20a%20Friend"><i>Betray a Friend</i></a> secret objective.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="starlancer"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mahact_Gene-Sorcerers#Mech:~:text=Starlancer">Starlancer</a> <sub>(Mech)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Starlancer must be in the system before activation to be able to use its ability.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If Mahact has an Arborec Command Token in their fleet pool &hellip; can the Mahact player produce a mech &hellip;? A: No, the mech was not in the system at the time of activation, so it didn&rsquo;t see the trigger for its ability.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Once the Mahact player resolves the ability of a Starlancer, the active player cannot use any &ldquo;after you activate a system&rdquo; abilities.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;In regards to the Mahact Commander, Il Na Viroset, when does your turn end? &hellip; Is this different from Nullification Field or Starlancer? A: &hellip; when/after you activate and other abilities within your turn cannot be used when the Mahact player places a second token in a system. End of turn abilities can still be used. Any ability that ends your turn should be treated as ending your turn when they occur, and no further abilities during that same trigger window can take place.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>Other players, including the Mahact player, cannot use any &ldquo;after another player activates a system that&hellip;&rdquo; abilities.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;In regards to the Mahact Commander, Il Na Viroset, when does your turn end? &hellip; Is this different from Nullification Field or Starlancer? A: &hellip; when/after you activate and other abilities within your turn cannot be used when the Mahact player places a second token in a system. End of turn abilities can still be used. Any ability that ends your turn should be treated as ending your turn when they occur, and no further abilities during that same trigger window can take place.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>The active player may still use any &ldquo;at the end of your turn&rdquo; abilities.<sup>4,6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;In regards to the Mahact Commander, Il Na Viroset, when does your turn end? &hellip; Is this different from Nullification Field or Starlancer? A: &hellip; when/after you activate and other abilities within your turn cannot be used when the Mahact player places a second token in a system. End of turn abilities can still be used. Any ability that ends your turn should be treated as ending your turn when they occur, and no further abilities during that same trigger window can take place.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;A previous ruling has stated that if an effect ends a player&rsquo;s turn, they may still use &lsquo;at the end of your turn&rsquo; abilities.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Mahact player may use the ability to end their own turn and gain their own spent command token from their fleet pool.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, &ldquo;Can Mahact use their mech ability on themselves?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Can Mahact use their mech ability on themselves? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="vaults-of-the-heir"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mahact_Gene-Sorcerers#Breakthrough:~:text=Vaults%20of%20the%20Heir">Vaults of the Heir</a> <sub>(Breakthrough)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The purged technology must be one that the Mahact player has in their play area, and not from their technology deck.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>The technology may be exhausted when it is purged.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>Once a technology has been purged, the Mahact player cannot regain it for the remainder of the game.<sup>7,8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook, Purge: &ldquo;If an ability instructs a player to purge a component, that component is removed from the game and returned to the box.&rdquo; purged component is out of the game.</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK rulebook: &ldquo;A purged card is removed from the&rdquo; game.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Mahact player purges the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Antimass_Deflectors"><i>Antimass Deflectors</i></a> technology, their units may remain in and move out of any asteroid fields they are currently in, but cannot move additional units into or through.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Mahact player purges their War Sun unit upgrade technology, each of their war suns are removed from the game board.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 90.20: &ldquo;If a Valefar Assimilator token is removed from a war sun unit upgrade and the Nekro Virus player does not have the standard war sun unit upgrade, each of the Nekro Virus player&rsquo;s war suns are returned to their reinforcements.&rdquo; By analogy: a player who loses their war sun unit upgrade loses their war suns.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
